pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% THE OPPOSITE-VERDICT COMPANION, same formula and same binary: what the instance actually
% is. The two hard clauses are `(x1)` and `(~x1)` — the second is written `-01`, which is
% the DIMACS literal -1 — so they resolve to the empty clause and the instance is
% INFEASIBLE. `conclusion BOUNDS INF INF` is the MaxSAT verdict for that.
%
% This proof only checks once the parser reads the literal's VALUE: with the token-text
% naming the two clauses were about DIFFERENT variables, so `pol 1 2 +` produced
% `+1 x1 +1 ~x01 >= 1` rather than the empty contradiction.
f 2;
pol 1 2 +;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS INF : 3 INF;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
